qbittorrent-nox 5.2.3
---------------------

rigseed distributes qbittorrent-nox as a sidecar process. The exact build is pinned
in sidecar.json.

  Upstream: https://github.com/qbittorrent/qBittorrent
  Tag:      release-5.2.3
  Licence:  GPL-3.0-or-later (binary distribution)

Upstream draws a distinction worth stating precisely. The qBittorrent source code is
GPL-2.0-or-later, but the binary distribution is GPL-3.0-or-later, because it bundles
GPLv3+ assets such as images. rigseed ships the binary, so GPL-3.0-or-later is the
licence that governs redistribution.

Both licence texts are included, along with the OpenSSL linking exception that upstream
adds in either case:

  licenses/qbittorrent/COPYING.txt          the exception and upstream's own summary
  licenses/qbittorrent/COPYING.GPLv2.txt
  licenses/qbittorrent/COPYING.GPLv3.txt

rigseed communicates with qbittorrent-nox only over its HTTP Web API v2.x, as a separate
process. No qBittorrent source is compiled into rigseed, and rigseed is not a derivative
work of it. rigseed's own licence is unaffected.

What the GPL does require is that anyone receiving the binary can obtain the matching
source. rigseed satisfies GPLv3 section 6(d) by attaching the corresponding source
archive to the same GitHub release that carries the binary. See licenses/README.md.

